# UMBRA Architecture Constraints

Source of truth: `.agent/PROJECT_GOAL.md`. This rule restates load-bearing constraints for coding agents.

## What we are building

The persistent organism and brain core for a believable autonomous digital pet companion. UMBRA is the internal life; avatars, robots, dialogue, animations, and sensors are bodies and interfaces around that life.

## Forbidden patterns

Do not implement:

- An LLM as the central controller (language may express; must not command)
- Scripted emotional responses or predefined personality performances
- Dependence on user prompts to remain active
- Direct commands such as become happy, bond, eat, play, sleep, or become afraid
- UMBRA-D-000A / chemistry-protocell reframes as a required foundation
- Behavior that stops solely because no user is present

## Required properties (design toward these)

- Persistent identity; continuous autonomous existence; homeostatic needs and regulation
- Internally generated action; learning from consequences; developmental change
- Selective long-term memory; habits and preferences; relationship formation
- Temperament shaped by history; coherent embodied expression
- Transfer between virtual and physical bodies
- Optional language that expresses rather than controls the organism

## Success criteria (do not claim success without evidence)

See the numbered success list in `.agent/PROJECT_GOAL.md`.

## Optional long-range research (non-gating)

Digital chemistry, protocells, autopoietic membranes, molecular metabolism, and bottom-up cellular reproduction may be investigated later. They must not gate the companion core or D-001.

